What is Aircraft Self-Protection Suite?
Aircraft Self-Protection Suite refers to integrated defensive systems designed to safeguard military and specialized commercial aircraft from evolving airborne and ground-based threats. These suites combine electronic warfare (EW) capabilities, directed infrared countermeasures (DIRCM), and traditional chaff and flare dispensers to detect, disrupt, and neutralize radar-guided and infrared-guided missiles. Modern conflict environments increasingly rely on advanced tracking and targeting technologies, requiring highly responsive and multi-layered defensive architectures. Key components such as missile warning sensors, laser-based DIRCM turrets, and digital radio-frequency memory (DRFM) jammers work together to reduce aircraft vulnerability.
